From 22ec6071bf2ca03ca25de7c1ecd794450acfba5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:35:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] [jakompiled] web: OpenGOAL's extractor in the browser
 (WasmFS + OPFS)

- extractor-web: decompiler/extractor/main.cpp without the compile/play steps, with WasmFS and its
  OPFS backend so the extracted ISO and decompiler output stay on disk, in the browser's private
  file system; decompiler config and texture assets embedded (no game data)
- decompiler builds for wasm32: xdelta3 SIZEOF_SIZE_T from the compiler, usize_t for xd3 sizes
- tiny_gltf keeps the web compile flags (its CMakeLists replaces CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS)
- extractor_util: the suggested ELF database entry had 4 format fields for 3 arguments
